I walk directly to the meat counter in the supermarket.
A butcher stands behind the glass counter.
He smiles and greets me.
"Hello, what can I get you?" he asks.
I need minced meat for my Bouletten.
"Hello."
"I would like mixed minced meat," I answer.
"Gladly."
"How much would you like?" the butcher asks.
"Exactly half a kilo, please," I say.
He takes some meat and puts it on the scale.
"That is five hundred and ten grams."
"Is that also okay?" he asks.
"Yes, that is perfect," I answer.
He wraps the meat in paper.
Then he sticks a label on it.
He hands me the package over the glass counter.
"Here you go."
"Do you need anything else?" he asks.
"No, thank you."
"That is all," I say.
I put the package in my shopping basket.
